sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: Any solid angle is contained by plane angles whose sum is less than four right angles.
----
proof:

Let the angle at {A} be a solid angle contained by the plane angles {BAC|angBAC}, {CAD|angCAD}, and {DAB|angDAB}.

I say that the sum of the angles {BAC|angBAC}, {CAD|angCAD}, and {DAB|angDAB} is less than four right angles.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="230" height="220" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XI.21 diagram" src="propXI21.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: the solid angle at A drawn as the three filled faces
    // ABC, ABD, ACD of a pyramid on the base BCD.
    //
    // Joyce draws AB, AC, AD and BC, CD, DB only as the edges of the
    // filled triangles. The walk needs the three edges at A before BC, CD,
    // DB are joined, so all six are solid slide twins, hidden at rest
    // (initiallyHidden), stroked from the end they are drawn from; the
    // triangles trace and fill when the proof turns to their angle sums.
    // ABCt, ACDt, ADBt are faceless twins of the filled triangles (a
    // highlighted face is raised over the markers, #140); the captions
    // route the triangles to them. The twelve angle markers are named
    // ang + Joyce's first spelling; triangle and angle names collide
    // (ABC, ADB), so the angles take the display override. Markers are
    // pinned to opt out of ring stepping: the three at A, and the two
    // face angles at B, C, D, lie side by side at 22; the base angles
    // CBD, BCD, CDB, which contain them, sit outside at 34.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B, C, D free. All four
    // are named by the setting-out, so none is deferred.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","C","D","AB","AC","AD"];
    var ATA   = ["angBAC","angCAD","angDAB"];
    var JOIN  = GIVEN.concat(["BC","CD","DB"]);
    var ATB   = ["angCBA","angABD","angCBD"];
    var ATC   = ["angBCA","angACD","angBCD"];
    var ATD   = ["angCDA","angADB","angCDB"];
    var SIX   = ["angCBA","angABD","angBCA","angACD","angCDA","angADB"];
    var THREE = ["angCBD","angBCD","angCDB"];
    var TRI   = JOIN.concat(["ABC","ABD","ACD"]);
    var TWINS = ["ABCt","ACDt","ADBt"];
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "XI.21",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;140,110",
            "B;point;free;40,180",
            "C;point;free;100,40",
            "D;point;free;190,130",
            "ABC;polygon;triangle;A,B,C;0;0;black;random",
            "ABD;polygon;triangle;A,B,D;0;0;black;random",
            "ACD;polygon;triangle;A,C,D;0;0;black;random",
            // Slide twins, hidden at rest (see above).
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "AC;line;connect;A,C",
            "AD;line;connect;A,D",
            "BC;line;connect;B,C",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D",
            "DB;line;connect;D,B",
            // Faceless highlight twins of the triangles. Explicit ;0 faces.
            "ABCt;polygon;triangle;A,B,C;0;0;0;0",
            "ACDt;polygon;triangle;A,C,D;0;0;0;0",
            "ADBt;polygon;triangle;A,D,B;0;0;0;0",
            "angBAC;sector;angleMarker;A,B,C,22",
            "angCAD;sector;angleMarker;A,C,D,22",
            "angDAB;sector;angleMarker;A,D,B,22",
            "angCBA;sector;angleMarker;B,C,A,22",
            "angABD;sector;angleMarker;B,A,D,22",
            "angCBD;sector;angleMarker;B,C,D,34",
            "angBCA;sector;angleMarker;C,B,A,22",
            "angACD;sector;angleMarker;C,A,D,22",
            "angBCD;sector;angleMarker;C,B,D,34",
            "angCDA;sector;angleMarker;D,C,A,22",
            "angADB;sector;angleMarker;D,A,B,22",
            "angCDB;sector;angleMarker;D,C,B,34"
        ],
        initiallyHidden: ["AB","AC","AD","BC","CD","DB"],
        slides: [
            { text: "“Any solid angle is contained by plane angles whose sum is less than four right angles.”",
              visible: GIVEN.concat(ATA),
              highlighted: ATA,
              justifications: [{ ref: "XI.21" }] },
            { text: "Let the angle at {A} be a solid angle contained by the plane angles {BAC|angBAC}, {CAD|angCAD}, and {DAB|angDAB}.",
              visible: GIVEN.concat(ATA),
              highlighted: ["A"].concat(ATA),
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angBAC", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angCAD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angDAB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "I say that the sum of the angles {BAC|angBAC}, {CAD|angCAD}, and {DAB|angDAB} is less than four right angles.",
              visible: GIVEN.concat(ATA),
              highlighted: ATA },
            { text: "Take points {B}, {C}, and {D} at random on the straight lines {AB}, {AC}, and {AD} respectively,",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["B","C","D","AB","AC","AD"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "B", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "C", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "D", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "and join {BC}, {CD}, and {DB}.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["BC","CD","DB"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "BC", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "CD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "DB", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "Now, since the solid angle at {B} is contained by the three plane angles {CBA|angCBA}, {ABD|angABD}, and {CBD|angCBD},",
              visible: JOIN.concat(ATB),
              highlighted: ["B"].concat(ATB),
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angCBA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angABD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angCBD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "and the sum of any two is greater than the remaining one,",
              visible: JOIN.concat(ATB),
              highlighted: ATB },
            { text: "therefore the sum of the angles {CBA|angCBA} and {ABD|angABD} is greater than the angle {CBD|angCBD}.",
              visible: JOIN.concat(ATB),
              highlighted: ATB,
              justifications: [{ claim: "CBA + ABD > CBD", ref: "XI.20" }] },
            { text: "For the same reason the sum of the angles {BCA|angBCA} and {ACD|angACD} is greater than the angle {BCD|angBCD},",
              visible: JOIN.concat(ATC),
              highlighted: ATC,
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angBCA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angACD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angBCD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "BCA + ACD > BCD", ref: "XI.20" }] },
            { text: "and the sum of the angles {CDA|angCDA} and {ADB|angADB} is greater than the angle {CDB|angCDB}.",
              visible: JOIN.concat(ATD),
              highlighted: ATD,
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angCDA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angADB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angCDB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "CDA + ADB > CDB", ref: "XI.20" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the sum of the six angles {CBA|angCBA}, {ABD|angABD}, {BCA|angBCA}, {ACD|angACD}, {CDA|angCDA}, and {ADB|angADB}",
              visible: JOIN.concat(SIX, THREE),
              highlighted: SIX },
            { text: "is greater than the sum of the three angles {CBD|angCBD}, {BCD|angBCD}, and {CDB|angCDB}.",
              visible: JOIN.concat(SIX, THREE),
              highlighted: THREE },
            { text: "But the sum of the three angles {CBD|angCBD}, {BDC|angCDB}, and {BCD|angBCD} equals two right angles,",
              visible: JOIN.concat(THREE),
              highlighted: ["BC","CD","DB"].concat(THREE),
              justifications: [{ claim: "angles of triangle BCD = 2 rt", ref: "I.32" }] },
            { text: "therefore the sum of the six angles {CBA|angCBA}, {ABD|angABD}, {BCA|angBCA}, {ACD|angACD}, {CDA|angCDA}, and {ADB|angADB} is greater than two right angles.",
              visible: JOIN.concat(SIX),
              highlighted: SIX },
            { text: "And, since the each sum of the three angles of the triangles {ABC|ABCt}, {ACD|ACDt}, and {ADB|ADBt} equals two right angles,",
              visible: TRI,
              highlighted: TWINS,
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "ABC", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "ACD", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "ABD", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "therefore the sum of the nine angles of the three triangles,",
              visible: TRI.concat(ATA, SIX),
              highlighted: TWINS },
            { text: "the angles {CBA|angCBA}, {ACB|angBCA}, {BAC|angBAC}, {ACD|angACD}, {CDA|angCDA}, {CAD|angCAD}, {ADB|angADB}, {DBA|angABD}, and {BAD|angDAB} equals six right angles.",
              visible: TRI.concat(ATA, SIX),
              highlighted: ATA.concat(SIX) },
            { text: "Of them the sum of the six angles {ABC|angCBA}, {BCA|angBCA}, {ACD|angACD}, {CDA|angCDA}, {ADB|angADB}, and {DBA|angABD} are greater than two right angles,",
              visible: TRI.concat(ATA, SIX),
              highlighted: SIX },
            { text: "therefore the sum of the remaining three angles {BAC|angBAC}, {CAD|angCAD}, and {DAB|angDAB} containing the solid angle is less than four right angles.",
              visible: TRI.concat(ATA),
              highlighted: ATA },
            { text: "Therefore, any solid angle is contained by plane angles whose sum is less than four right angles.",
              visible: TRI.concat(ATA),
              highlighted: ATA,
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "XI.21") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.Post.1": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post1/",
        "I.32":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI32/",
        "XI.20":    "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI20/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Take points {B}, {C}, and {D} at random on the straight lines {AB}, {AC}, and {AD} respectively, and join {BC}, {CD}, and {DB}.

Now, since the solid angle at {B} is contained by the three plane angles {CBA|angCBA}, {ABD|angABD}, and {CBD|angCBD}, and the sum of any two is greater than the remaining one, therefore the sum of the angles {CBA|angCBA} and {ABD|angABD} is greater than the angle {CBD|angCBD}. [!just XI.20]

For the same reason the sum of the angles {BCA|angBCA} and {ACD|angACD} is greater than the angle {BCD|angBCD}, and the sum of the angles {CDA|angCDA} and {ADB|angADB} is greater than the angle {CDB|angCDB}. Therefore the sum of the six angles {CBA|angCBA}, {ABD|angABD}, {BCA|angBCA}, {ACD|angACD}, {CDA|angCDA}, and {ADB|angADB} is greater than the sum of the three angles {CBD|angCBD}, {BCD|angBCD}, and {CDB|angCDB}.

But the sum of the three angles {CBD|angCBD}, {BDC|angCDB}, and {BCD|angBCD} equals two right angles, therefore the sum of the six angles {CBA|angCBA}, {ABD|angABD}, {BCA|angBCA}, {ACD|angACD}, {CDA|angCDA}, and {ADB|angADB} is greater than two right angles. [!just I.32]

And, since the each sum of the three angles of the triangles {ABC|ABCt}, {ACD|ACDt}, and {ADB|ADBt} equals two right angles, therefore the sum of the nine angles of the three triangles, the angles {CBA|angCBA}, {ACB|angBCA}, {BAC|angBAC}, {ACD|angACD}, {CDA|angCDA}, {CAD|angCAD}, {ADB|angADB}, {DBA|angABD}, and {BAD|angDAB} equals six right angles. Of them the sum of the six angles {ABC|angCBA}, {BCA|angBCA}, {ACD|angACD}, {CDA|angCDA}, {ADB|angADB}, and {DBA|angABD} are greater than two right angles, therefore the sum of the remaining three angles {BAC|angBAC}, {CAD|angCAD}, and {DAB|angDAB} containing the solid angle is less than four right angles.

Therefore, *any solid angle is contained by plane angles whose sum is less than four right angles.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide:

In proposition @XI.23 the condition stated here and the condition in @XI.20 (the sum of any two plane angles is less than the third) together are shown to be sufficient to construct a solid angle.

#### About the proof

The proof only shows that the sum of the plane angles in all cases is less than four right angles when there are three plane angles, not when there are more than three. When there are four ore more plane angles, the proof is analogous, but it is necessary to invoke Proclus' <a href="/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI32/#cor1">first corollary</a> to I.32, which states "the sum of the interior angles of a convex rectilinear figure equals twice as many angles as the figure has sides, less four."

#### Use of this proposition

This proposition is used in the proof of the <a href="/elements/books/bookXIII/propositions/propXIII18/#remark">remark</a> after proposition XIII.18 to show that the five regular polyhedra constructed in Book XIII are the only five possible.
